<section>
  <div class="tight">
    <h2>The gap in the middle</h2>
    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <p class="lede" style="max-width:none">Intent for a trip is created long before anyone opens a search bar. It happens in a Reel at 11pm, in a Story someone screenshots, in a two-year-old TikTok about a town nobody had heard of. By the time a traveller reaches a booking page, the decision is largely made — and the platform that takes 20% of it had nothing to do with making it.</p>
        <p class="lede" style="max-width:none;margin-top:1.1rem">Meanwhile the person who actually created that intent gets paid in exposure, or gets a flat fee that has no relationship to what the post did. And the independent property paying the toll never learns which content brought them a guest.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <ul class="ticks">
          <li><b>Creators</b> monetise everything about travel except the travel itself</li>
          <li><b>Properties</b> pay the most for the guests they're least able to keep</li>
          <li><b>Travellers</b> book somewhere worse than what they were shown, because it was easier</li>
          <li><b>Nobody</b> holds the record that connects the content to the booking</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band-mist">
  <div class="tight">
    <h2>What FETCH is</h2>
    <p class="lede">An attribution and commission layer for direct travel bookings. A creator tags a place in content they already made; a traveller taps through and books direct on the property's own engine; the booking is verified; the creator gets paid in cash on the completed stay.</p>
    <div class="cards">
      <div class="card"><span class="n">1</span><h3>Not a marketplace</h3><p>We don't want travellers browsing FETCH. We want them booking you, direct, from the content that inspired them.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="n">2</span><h3>Not a booking engine</h3><p>The property's engine takes the booking. FETCH doesn't compete with it and never will.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="n">3</span><h3>Not an advertising product</h3><p>Nothing is charged for reach, impressions or placement. If no booking happens, nobody pays anything.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="n">4</span><h3>Invisible infrastructure</h3><p>The traveller never learns FETCH exists. The best version of this product is one nobody sees.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="tight">
    <h2>Four rules we don't break</h2>
    <div class="cards">
      <div class="card"><h3>Never hold the money</h3><p>FETCH never touches the traveller's payment and never becomes merchant of record. The property is paid directly, always.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>Never become a destination</h3><p>No competing booking engine, no consumer marketplace. The moment travellers search FETCH instead of you, we've broken the model.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>Never charge to join</h3><p>No listing fees, no subscriptions, no charge for hosted stays. Free for both sides, permanently.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>Never creep the take rate</h3><p>10%, split evenly. New fees would make FETCH another toll — which is the thing it was built to remove.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band-sky">
  <div class="tight">
    <h2>Where we are right now</h2>
    <p class="lede">Pilot phase, and deliberately unglamorous. The whole job at this stage is answering one question honestly.</p>
    <div class="rail-steps">
      <div class="rail-step"><span class="pillx">Now</span><b>Prove the number</b><p>One vertical on the BC coast. Ten properties, a handful of creators, every pairing set up and verified by hand. Promo codes and a simple tracked link — no platform required.</p></div>
      <div class="rail-step"><span class="pillx">Next</span><b>Automate the proof</b><p>Conversion pixel plus PMS webhooks (Guesty, Hostaway), instant commission splits, and creator self-serve across the whole network.</p></div>
      <div class="rail-step"><span class="pillx">Then</span><b>Scale through the pipes</b><p>PMS app marketplaces — one integration reaching thousands of properties — and publishing the conversion data the pilot produced.</p></div>
      <div class="rail-step"><span class="pillx">Always</span><b>Density before coverage</b><p>Twenty bookable places in one region beats two hundred scattered. Each region gets proven before the next one opens.</p></div>
    </div>
    <p class="calc-note" style="margin-top:1.6rem">The question the pilot answers: does creator content convert to direct bookings at a rate that pays everyone? If the honest answer is no, that's worth knowing early.</p>
  </div>
</section>

